{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00362",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.65,
      "end_seconds": 9.83,
      "duration_seconds": 9.18,
      "text": "Hi doctor, um, sorry, the lift was out and I had to take the stairs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.87,
      "end_seconds": 16.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.66,
      "text": "So, no trouble at all, come in. What's been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 21.43,
      "end_seconds": 25.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "Well, I've been having pain on swallowing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 27.99,
      "end_seconds": 44.44,
      "duration_seconds": 16.45,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. BP is 110 over 77, respiratory rate 21. Temp 38.1 degrees, BMI works out to 27.8, height 175 centimetres, pulse 104, weight 85 kilos, saturation 96 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.34,
      "end_seconds": 49.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Okay, noted. When did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.68,
      "end_seconds": 52.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Probably three days. Yeah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.47,
      "end_seconds": 61.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Is there anything that triggers it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.13,
      "end_seconds": 67.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "Yes, swallowing. That makes it worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.83,
      "end_seconds": 71.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "Has there been a very sore throat too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.14,
      "end_seconds": 77.77,
      "duration_seconds": 5.63,
      "text": "Yeah, that too. As for very sore throat, I'd call it mild."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.6,
      "end_seconds": 81.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "Have you had a fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.53,
      "end_seconds": 91.81,
      "duration_seconds": 8.28,
      "text": "Yes, for about a week. With fever, I'd say severe. There's swollen glands in the neck as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.52,
      "end_seconds": 95.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "How bad is it, would you say?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.6,
      "end_seconds": 102.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "Maybe a three out of ten on a bad day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.14,
      "end_seconds": 113.01,
      "duration_seconds": 5.87,
      "text": "Have you had pain on swallowing before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.2,
      "end_seconds": 125.13,
      "duration_seconds": 6.93,
      "text": "Hmm, I had a similar thing about six months ago. It went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.44,
      "end_seconds": 134.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "Did you get rash, ear pain or difficulty breathing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.33,
      "end_seconds": 140.55,
      "duration_seconds": 5.22,
      "text": "No rash, ear pain or difficulty breathing, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.12,
      "end_seconds": 145.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "A few quick ones: cough, runny nose or drooling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.28,
      "end_seconds": 151.47,
      "duration_seconds": 5.19,
      "text": "So, I haven't had cough, runny nose or drooling, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.19,
      "end_seconds": 157.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.91,
      "end_seconds": 161.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "No, that side's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.53,
      "end_seconds": 180.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.7,
      "end_seconds": 185.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "Oh, no, nothing I'm aware of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.59,
      "end_seconds": 188.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Have you got any chronic problems?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.98,
      "end_seconds": 195.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.7,
      "text": "Asthma, for two years. I have an underactive thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.53,
      "end_seconds": 199.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "Okay, and what else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.2,
      "end_seconds": 209.98,
      "duration_seconds": 8.78,
      "text": "I have an irregular heartbeat, for about a year. I've had arthritis in my knees, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.17,
      "end_seconds": 220.09,
      "duration_seconds": 8.92,
      "text": "Yes, asthma and an underactive thyroid are known to us, good to have that clear. A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.43,
      "end_seconds": 234.17,
      "duration_seconds": 12.74,
      "text": "I walk for about half an hour most days. I drive a delivery van all day. I share a flat with two friends."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.42,
      "end_seconds": 252.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "What's your current medication list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.63,
      "end_seconds": 262.34,
      "duration_seconds": 7.71,
      "text": "Seretide inhaler, twice a day. Thyroxine. I take it 75 micrograms, maybe, every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.68,
      "end_seconds": 267.72,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Did you happen to bring the box or the paperwork?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 269.38,
      "end_seconds": 275.53,
      "duration_seconds": 6.15,
      "text": "No, it's at home. Diclofenac. I take it 50 milligrams, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 277.18,
      "end_seconds": 282.07,
      "duration_seconds": 4.89,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 25 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.29,
      "end_seconds": 289.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Right. Do you happen to have the current prescription here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 290.46,
      "end_seconds": 295.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.28,
      "text": "No, I left it at home. I take paracetamol, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.93,
      "end_seconds": 299.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "How much do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.95,
      "end_seconds": 305.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "It's 500 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.43,
      "end_seconds": 309.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Come over here and I'll have a look."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.72,
      "end_seconds": 313.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Let me look at this properly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.56,
      "end_seconds": 327.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "The glands under the jaw are tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.21,
      "end_seconds": 331.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Take your time, no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.25,
      "end_seconds": 349.3,
      "duration_seconds": 6.05,
      "text": "Both tonsils are red and swollen, and there are white patches on the left one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 351.96,
      "end_seconds": 354.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "That's all I need, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 363.93,
      "end_seconds": 380.27,
      "duration_seconds": 16.34,
      "text": "Okay, thinking it through, it fits best with tonsillitis, probably bacterial. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more. I can't rule out a viral throat infection yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 381.29,
      "end_seconds": 384.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "What are the chances it's something bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 385.34,
      "end_seconds": 407.58,
      "duration_seconds": 22.24,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now tonsillitis, probably bacterial is my leading thought, not anything worse. I'd like to arrange a throat swab for sore throat. I'll start you on amoxicillin, 500 milligrams, three times a day, for five days. It's for throat infection."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 408.74,
      "end_seconds": 409.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.04,
      "text": "Right, understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 410.81,
      "end_seconds": 426.19,
      "duration_seconds": 15.38,
      "text": "Finish the whole course of antibiotics even if you feel better after two days. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 427.64,
      "end_seconds": 429.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "Okay, I'll remember."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 430.52,
      "end_seconds": 443.04,
      "duration_seconds": 12.52,
      "text": "If you can't swallow your saliva or you have trouble breathing, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department. Book a review in a week. Look after yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 444.7,
      "end_seconds": 449.92,
      "duration_seconds": 5.22,
      "text": "I think that's clear. Thank you for being so thorough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 451.65,
      "end_seconds": 452.92,
      "duration_seconds": 1.27,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}